WEBVTT

00:04.900 --> 00:06.530
What the hell is this place?!

00:06.770 --> 00:09.900
If you are destined to be a shard caster,

00:09.900 --> 00:12.810
then you will soon have need
of what I've given you.

00:13.010 --> 00:16.640
The more elite shard casters
have stronger spirits.

00:21.620 --> 00:26.080
Come on, tell me.

00:26.620 --> 00:29.920
Are you my spirit?

00:31.760 --> 00:39.500
We've all surely got our arms outstretched

00:39.500 --> 00:46.460
Towards a far, faraway place

00:59.820 --> 01:06.030
Blown by the wind, we walk on

01:06.030 --> 01:12.990
Wanting to know the reason we were born

01:13.200 --> 01:19.510
Even if a time of loss should come

01:19.510 --> 01:26.640
Let's now choose to hold each other tight

01:29.080 --> 01:36.490
We've all surely got our arms outstretched

01:36.490 --> 01:42.460
Towards something we can't lose

01:42.460 --> 01:50.110
Pulling only brilliant dreams closer

01:50.110 --> 01:56.980
Towards a far, faraway place

02:04.790 --> 02:08.810
Episode 3
Those With Power

02:13.500 --> 02:15.530
You cause yet another
disturbance trying to escape

02:15.530 --> 02:18.160
before the assault charges against
you have even been cleared.

02:18.700 --> 02:21.600
Roya was been cleared of all suspicions,

02:21.600 --> 02:24.570
but the Council will not remain silent
over last night's incident.

02:25.110 --> 02:27.070
Just what do you intend to do?

02:27.510 --> 02:32.310
Elder Zico, this is your fault
for letting him go free.

02:32.610 --> 02:35.910
Well, boy? Did you sense anything?

02:38.690 --> 02:41.020
You look quite exhausted.

02:41.020 --> 02:46.820
It takes a great deal of power when one
is not skilled at controlling spirits.

02:51.030 --> 02:54.660
Is that thing a spirit? Is it my spirit?

02:55.200 --> 02:56.830
Correct.

02:57.370 --> 03:03.170
However, you are far from having what
it takes to truly make it your own.

03:06.610 --> 03:08.580
What it takes?

03:09.750 --> 03:13.550
Boy, would you consider going to see Dumas?

03:14.560 --> 03:16.180
Dumas?

03:21.260 --> 03:22.900
Him, huh?

03:22.900 --> 03:28.030
He is strong, an elite shard caster.

03:37.080 --> 03:41.050
I do indeed sense something in him.

03:41.050 --> 03:43.950
The boy is truly outrageous.

03:43.950 --> 03:47.260
Shouldn't he be trained by you?

03:47.260 --> 03:49.390
There is no need.

03:49.390 --> 03:52.690
He will carve out his destiny on his own.

03:54.100 --> 03:57.060
He has the power to do so.

04:09.440 --> 04:10.650
I'm right here!

04:10.650 --> 04:11.750
Catch me if you can!

04:11.750 --> 04:13.880
Come on, Master Robès!

04:13.880 --> 04:14.880
Here I am!

04:14.880 --> 04:16.510
Wrong one!

04:16.720 --> 04:18.250
Got you!

04:18.250 --> 04:19.820
Huh?

04:19.820 --> 04:21.450
There!

04:22.160 --> 04:24.930
Such a sturdy embrace...

04:24.930 --> 04:27.330
This soothing, fragrant scent is...

04:27.330 --> 04:29.460
Me, sir.

04:29.960 --> 04:31.570
What, it's you?

04:31.570 --> 04:32.900
What brings you here all of a sudden?

04:32.900 --> 04:35.700
Sir, my apologies for interrupting
you while at leisure.

04:35.700 --> 04:38.000
It's a matter concerning the boy.

04:38.910 --> 04:40.070
Really?!

04:40.070 --> 04:41.780
Oh, dear...

04:41.780 --> 04:43.180
I see...

04:43.180 --> 04:45.150
Yet more entertainment to look forward to.

04:45.980 --> 04:48.110
Jeeves, make preparations for a party!

04:48.550 --> 04:51.680
All of you enjoy yourselves
as much as you can!

04:52.590 --> 04:54.210
Wonderful!

05:07.600 --> 05:10.730
Oh, that's it, Dumas's house.

05:11.240 --> 05:13.010
Oh, it's Mickey!

05:13.010 --> 05:13.710
Who's that?

05:13.710 --> 05:15.480
Dumas's pupil.
Who's that?

05:15.480 --> 05:17.100
Mickey!

05:17.580 --> 05:19.150
That's Roya!

05:19.150 --> 05:22.280
Roya! Long time, no see!

05:23.150 --> 05:24.420
That mark on his cheek...

05:24.420 --> 05:25.020
Hey, Roya!
That mark on his cheek...

05:25.020 --> 05:27.320
Hey, Roya!
Is he also a shard caster?

05:30.390 --> 05:32.830
I'll bet you're surprised to see
what a mess the house is.

05:32.830 --> 05:37.130
He may be the shard champion, but all
he gets out of that is a fancy title.

05:37.130 --> 05:40.260
Which means he's got to support
himself by other means.

05:40.740 --> 05:42.860
Oh, look, there he is.

05:43.340 --> 05:47.140
That's my teacher, Dumas,
working out in the field.

05:48.780 --> 05:50.400
Oh, you idiot!

06:06.930 --> 06:09.260
That's the boy who came from
another world, right?

06:09.260 --> 06:10.800
How did you know about him?

06:10.800 --> 06:14.240
Master Sebastian was here yesterday
talking about him with my teacher.

06:14.240 --> 06:15.770
I see...

06:15.770 --> 06:18.240
He's not a shard caster, is he?

06:18.910 --> 06:22.030
He's real sloppy, but I sense
great strength in him.

06:22.640 --> 06:25.610
If he starts training with my teacher,
I'm sure he'll become stronger.

06:52.410 --> 06:54.200
Is that all you've got?

06:54.640 --> 06:57.940
You've got other issues to worry
about before shard casting.

07:02.880 --> 07:04.510
Damn it...

07:09.920 --> 07:10.930
Here!

07:10.930 --> 07:13.360
You'll be training here from now on, won't you?

07:13.360 --> 07:15.800
So, that means field work for starters.

07:15.800 --> 07:18.370
Physical fitness is part of the basics
for shard casters too.

07:18.370 --> 07:20.000
Listen to me!

07:20.000 --> 07:22.440
Does he have a spirit too?

07:22.440 --> 07:24.110
Huh? You mean Teacher?

07:24.110 --> 07:25.410
Of course he does!

07:25.410 --> 07:27.310
The strongest of spirits!

07:27.310 --> 07:28.810
Hey, wait!

07:28.810 --> 07:30.940
Hey, what about training?

07:32.150 --> 07:33.210
Is it okay to let him go?

07:33.210 --> 07:34.680
Why not?
Is it okay to let him go?

07:51.130 --> 07:53.070
So nice to meet you, young man.

07:53.070 --> 07:54.860
Wh..Who are you?

07:58.440 --> 08:01.240
Whoa, whoa! That's Master Robès, in the flesh!

08:01.240 --> 08:03.510
Oh, what should I do?!

08:03.510 --> 08:05.080
You want something?

08:05.080 --> 08:07.680
I'm having a party at my place this evening.

08:07.680 --> 08:09.180
You are invited.

08:09.180 --> 08:10.620
What's with this all of a sudden?

08:10.620 --> 08:11.820
Sorry, not interested.

08:11.820 --> 08:14.620
I, however, am interested...

08:14.620 --> 08:17.590
In you, the boy who came from another world.

08:20.260 --> 08:23.130
It's a party for shard casters, you see.

08:23.130 --> 08:25.330
I believe you'll be able to enjoy yourself.

08:25.330 --> 08:28.600
Bring your friends over there.

08:28.600 --> 08:30.400
Well, see you.

08:33.770 --> 08:35.180
I'll be waiting!

08:35.180 --> 08:36.970
Come, let's go.

08:39.910 --> 08:42.380
Oh, Master Robès is magnificent!

08:43.380 --> 08:46.190
That's the first time I've seen his spirit.

08:46.190 --> 08:48.290
So, he's a shard caster too?

08:48.290 --> 08:51.490
We wouldn't miss your party for the world!

08:51.490 --> 08:52.530
Right?

08:52.530 --> 08:54.500
Go on your own if you want.

08:55.330 --> 08:56.930
Hey, we can't do that!

08:56.930 --> 08:58.470
You're the one who was invited,

08:58.470 --> 09:01.140
so it's not like the two of us can just
go by ourselves without you!

09:01.140 --> 09:02.140
Like I care.

09:02.140 --> 09:04.370
C'mon! You can go to a little party, can't you?

09:04.370 --> 09:06.910
I'm not interested in parties and crap!

09:06.910 --> 09:08.710
Leave me alone!

09:34.000 --> 09:36.640
I'm glad you could make it, Zed.

09:36.640 --> 09:39.510
Roya told me your name.

09:39.510 --> 09:40.940
Well, I was hungry.

09:40.940 --> 09:42.610
I owe you, man.

09:42.610 --> 09:44.310
Thank you very much.

09:44.310 --> 09:45.410
Not at all!

09:45.410 --> 09:48.180
I am just glad our food is to your liking.

09:48.180 --> 09:51.390
But how could you have gone to that Dumas?

09:51.390 --> 09:54.890
He's truly an uninteresting man,
if ever there was one!

09:54.890 --> 09:58.130
Spending his days tilling the soil so tediously...

09:58.130 --> 10:00.250
It's foolishness beyond compare, I tell you!

10:00.700 --> 10:03.260
Why, if it isn't Master Robès!

10:03.260 --> 10:06.800
Thank you kindly for your invitation tonight.

10:06.800 --> 10:10.840
And a most festive party it is, as always!

10:10.840 --> 10:13.810
Your words make me as glad as anyone here.

10:14.410 --> 10:19.250
Incidentally, Master Robès, you won't sit
out the Joust again this year, will you?

10:19.250 --> 10:22.180
Ah, yes, that has been the talk of the town!

10:22.180 --> 10:26.140
Everyone is saying that, if you enter,
you will far outshine Lord Dumas.

10:29.890 --> 10:35.860
For me, I'm afraid winning the championship
holds no significance or worth.

10:35.860 --> 10:38.370
You don't say? That's too bad...

10:38.370 --> 10:41.000
Hey, Mickey, Mr. Dumas is here.

10:41.000 --> 10:41.840
Here...

10:41.840 --> 10:42.440
What?
Here...

10:42.440 --> 10:43.700
What?
It's Dumas!

10:43.700 --> 10:45.170
He's the shard champion, isn't he?

10:45.170 --> 10:46.170
What is he doing here?

10:46.170 --> 10:48.140
How unusual to see him here.

10:51.710 --> 10:53.250
Well, well!

10:53.250 --> 10:55.720
I did not expect the Champion to
grace us with his presence!

10:55.720 --> 10:57.520
I am honored.

10:57.520 --> 10:58.990
You see, I had thought a party like this

10:58.990 --> 11:02.320
might be a bit above the level of
a farmer such as yourself.

11:02.320 --> 11:07.960
Or has the fame of being shard
champion gone to your head?

11:13.400 --> 11:16.870
I know! What say we have a little
sparring match right now?

11:16.870 --> 11:21.830
There are those here who are curious to
see which of us is the stronger.

11:24.980 --> 11:27.750
It would make for splendid entertainment.

11:27.750 --> 11:28.750
What do you say?

11:28.750 --> 11:32.210
Perhaps you should postpone
this until another day?

11:32.950 --> 11:34.060
Jeeves!

11:34.060 --> 11:37.490
I asked Master Dumas to come.

11:37.490 --> 11:38.630
What is the meaning of this?

11:38.630 --> 11:42.430
I wanted to speak to him regarding the matter
of the land you're lending him.

11:43.200 --> 11:45.500
If you would, Master Dumas.

11:52.310 --> 11:54.210
A pity...

11:54.210 --> 11:57.340
I wanted to show them who is stronger.

12:45.260 --> 12:48.000
Is that all you've got?

12:48.000 --> 12:51.450
You've got other issues to worry
about before shard casting.

12:52.900 --> 12:54.530
Damn!

13:03.940 --> 13:05.570
That mark!

13:07.410 --> 13:09.380
It's the same as the others'.

13:35.480 --> 13:37.710
Huh? Zed?

13:37.710 --> 13:39.680
What are you doing here?

13:39.680 --> 13:42.150
I chased some shady-looking guy here.

13:42.150 --> 13:43.950
I lost him right around here.

13:43.950 --> 13:44.950
Huh?

13:44.950 --> 13:47.420
What are you doing out here so late?

13:47.990 --> 13:52.450
Um... Uh, well, I still had some work
I needed to take care of.

13:54.230 --> 13:55.260
What is this place?

13:55.260 --> 13:57.930
It's Mr. Dumas's nursery.

13:57.930 --> 14:01.390
He, uh, cultivates all sorts of flowers here.

14:03.100 --> 14:04.900
Go ahead and bring him in.

14:05.210 --> 14:06.610
Teacher?

14:06.610 --> 14:09.080
No point trying to hide it.

14:16.180 --> 14:20.810
This is where Teacher treats people who can't
go to the hospital for certain reasons.

14:21.920 --> 14:24.220
He does it by using healing shards.

14:25.030 --> 14:29.330
He built this hospital all on his own
underneath the flower nursery.

14:35.640 --> 14:37.600
Dumas, these guys are...

14:38.440 --> 14:40.910
Zed, come with me a minute.

14:43.040 --> 14:46.850
Those guys are indeed Zymotan
soldiers, the enemy.

14:46.850 --> 14:50.580
But they're human beings, no different from us.

14:50.580 --> 14:53.720
If people are hurt, I heal them regardless
of whether they're friend or foe.

14:53.720 --> 14:56.190
What is wrong with that?

14:58.260 --> 15:03.860
Zymot is a land that's utterly dominated
by power and lust.

15:03.860 --> 15:09.170
Anyone like the people here, who were
defeated in combat, will be exiled.

15:09.670 --> 15:13.300
But these people also need a place to live.

15:14.380 --> 15:16.840
But they're the enemy, right?

15:25.420 --> 15:26.490
Here!

15:26.490 --> 15:29.790
He says it's late, so you need
to stay here tonight.

15:34.530 --> 15:35.730
The time is right.

15:35.730 --> 15:37.130
Then, we'll proceed as planned.

15:37.130 --> 15:39.760
Right, we make our move tomorrow night.

16:06.890 --> 16:08.530
Mom...

16:08.530 --> 16:10.500
I wonder if she's doing all right?

16:21.140 --> 16:22.310
Thank you.

16:22.310 --> 16:23.680
No prob.

16:23.680 --> 16:26.650
You're not from here, are you?

16:28.450 --> 16:31.690
In that case, it would be better if
you didn't hang around.

16:31.690 --> 16:33.980
Your mother's worried about you too.

16:38.630 --> 16:39.760
Morning, Mickey.

16:39.760 --> 16:41.890
Oh, good morning!

16:45.430 --> 16:49.840
Master Zico, are you familiar with
that spirit of Zed's?

16:49.840 --> 16:52.670
So, that's what you wanted to speak about, eh?

16:52.670 --> 16:55.110
I felt an unusual power...

16:55.110 --> 16:56.940
It was the first time I've seen a spirit like that.

16:57.850 --> 17:00.250
Who is Zed?

17:00.250 --> 17:02.650
What has he come here for?

17:02.650 --> 17:05.220
Are you really so concerned about Zed?

17:05.220 --> 17:07.390
Uh... It's not like that!

17:07.390 --> 17:10.360
It's just... just...

17:12.430 --> 17:14.720
I have a bad feeling...

17:16.600 --> 17:18.700
You know what I think, Roya?

17:18.700 --> 17:21.970
Things are bound to happen as they will.

17:21.970 --> 17:26.170
All is fate, including that boy coming here.

17:26.170 --> 17:28.640
Fate?

17:29.480 --> 17:31.270
Excuse me.

17:36.480 --> 17:38.520
Is something the matter?

17:38.520 --> 17:41.090
She's a bit flustered.

17:41.090 --> 17:44.020
She is most concerned about the boy.

17:44.020 --> 17:46.890
Being without a single relative,

17:46.890 --> 17:51.500
perhaps she sees something of herself in Zed,
who's come all alone from another world.

17:51.500 --> 17:53.900
She's such a considerate individual.

17:53.900 --> 17:56.470
It would be best to leave the boy alone.

17:56.470 --> 17:57.500
However, Roya...

17:57.500 --> 17:58.770
Yes, I understand.

17:58.770 --> 18:02.230
I understand perfectly well, Elder Zico.

18:04.210 --> 18:05.910
So you say...

18:05.910 --> 18:07.980
Well, what did you want?

18:07.980 --> 18:08.980
Oh, right!

18:08.980 --> 18:11.090
I received word from the Council.

18:11.090 --> 18:13.990
They've heard all about Zed.

18:13.990 --> 18:15.560
They will not let the matter go.

18:15.560 --> 18:18.060
Dimitri Khan, eh?

18:18.060 --> 18:21.900
I believe it's your job to handle that.

18:21.900 --> 18:25.020
Do you mean to cop out on me again?

18:34.710 --> 18:36.340
Yes?

18:37.180 --> 18:39.580
Roya! C'mon in!

18:39.580 --> 18:40.880
Huh? You're alone?

18:40.880 --> 18:43.510
Yeah, teacher went out earlier.

18:43.920 --> 18:46.890
Zed's been staying over at the
nursery since yesterday.

18:47.690 --> 18:49.320
Oh...

19:13.050 --> 19:14.450
Who is it?

19:14.450 --> 19:16.080
You?!

19:22.220 --> 19:24.350
Won't you reconsider?

19:25.190 --> 19:29.820
I've been waiting anxiously for this opportunity.

19:30.200 --> 19:34.160
I'm indebted to you, but I will take your life now.

19:43.340 --> 19:44.970
What is it?

19:46.110 --> 19:48.080
It's coming from the castle!

19:52.690 --> 19:53.850
What is it?

19:53.850 --> 19:55.480
It's begun.

19:59.660 --> 20:01.360
What do you think you're doing?

20:01.360 --> 20:03.990
We are people without any purpose.

20:04.530 --> 20:07.660
Life will be no different for us here in Templar.

20:08.240 --> 20:10.530
We have nowhere to go!

20:11.610 --> 20:15.560
That leaves us with only one choice:
to create our own place to live!

20:17.310 --> 20:20.110
I told you not to stay here!

20:26.220 --> 20:28.520
The enemy! Zymotan soldiers!

20:30.320 --> 20:32.490
Huh? That woman...

20:32.490 --> 20:33.760
It couldn't be!

20:33.760 --> 20:35.390
No way!

20:40.500 --> 20:42.130
Damn it...

20:43.240 --> 20:45.310
We'll have to do something about them.

20:45.310 --> 20:46.070
But...

20:46.070 --> 20:47.700
The gate's opening!
But...

20:56.750 --> 20:58.380
Master Robès!

21:00.520 --> 21:02.790
I haven't been so excited in some time.

21:02.790 --> 21:05.260
Is this what they mean by "raring to go"?

21:06.930 --> 21:09.050
Do not falter! We'll take him all at once!

21:20.170 --> 21:21.800
Go!

21:27.850 --> 21:29.480
Belladonna!

21:42.330 --> 21:43.960
Teacher!

21:54.170 --> 21:55.800
Dumas...

22:22.500 --> 22:26.460
This is the power of shard casters...

22:50.460 --> 22:54.330
I want to peak inside your heart, and find
out your feelings and expressions

22:54.330 --> 22:58.240
I see you bearing your burden alone, and don't
ask the reason for your twinkling tears

22:58.240 --> 23:01.810
I give you a shout of support without mentioning
them, between the answers I'm looking for

23:01.810 --> 23:05.940
Without obsessing or over thinking,
I feel sunbeams in the future you

23:07.650 --> 23:09.480
It feels nice, very, very much

23:09.480 --> 23:11.280
You and me, we're very, very good

23:11.280 --> 23:15.160
I'd like to be there for you any time

23:15.160 --> 23:16.990
Very, very much, whenever

23:16.990 --> 23:18.830
Very, very good, not changing

23:18.830 --> 23:24.790
We're always blooming full of hope,
with all our might (Oh)

23:30.300 --> 23:32.770
I feel this kindness amidst my doubt

23:34.070 --> 23:36.540
I will always have faith in you at all times

23:37.810 --> 23:41.720
Here in this vast landscape
under the sunny blue sky

23:41.720 --> 23:45.850
We got good feelings, good social standing,
we're good; I want to always be here

23:47.320 --> 23:49.120
It feels nice, very, very much

23:49.120 --> 23:50.960
You and me, we're very, very good

23:50.960 --> 23:54.760
I'd like to be there for you any time

23:54.760 --> 23:56.630
Very, very much, whenever

23:56.630 --> 23:58.500
Very, very good, not changing

23:58.500 --> 24:04.460
We're always blooming full of hope,
with all our might (Oh)

24:17.050 --> 24:19.950
Next time, "The Wind's Resolve"

24:17.580 --> 24:19.950
Next Time
The Wind's Resolve
